{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Source-Master project coordination for REAPER on shared storage.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Requires REAPER 7.74 or newer and ReaImGui 0.9 or newer (install ReaImGui through ReaPack).\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 ReaProjectLink\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 ReaProjectLink provides Source-Master project coordination for REAPER on shared storage.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 It is intended for game-audio cinematic production where dialogue, music, and sound-design teams work in separate REAPER projects and periodically deliver rendered audio into a Master Project. It uses an existing NAS rather than a cloud service or central project database, and it does not attempt to make multiple users edit the same REAPER project.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The working principle is:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Source Projects keep their own folder structures and working conventions;\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Source Teams explicitly publish bounced audio as versioned Deliveries;\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab the Master Project subscribes to Deliveries and manages downstream imports;\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab synchronization replaces Source-managed Items with a complete Delivery snapshot;\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab the Master Project publishes the shared Reference back to Source Projects.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Installation\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Install {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reapack.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
ReaPack
}}}
 and ReaImGui, then in REAPER choose Extensions > ReaPack > Import repositories and add:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 https://github.com/SounDoer/ReaProjectLink/raw/master/index.xml\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Install ReaProjectLink from Extensions > ReaPack > Browse packages. It appears in the Action List as {\f1 Script: ReaProjectLink.lua}.\par}
